  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi></math> and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> moves in a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> around an infinitely long line charge of linear density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></math>. Then time period will be given as:<br/>(Consider <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> as Coulomb's constant)",
    "image": null
  },
